    Do not hold generation off for a second when a swapchain is created (V443)
    
    Issue 19 on V441: the long dips to about 50 fps on a Steam Frame (Skyrim VR,
    Mad God's Overhaul, SteamVR 72 Hz, D3D11 bridge, NVIDIA) still came, later.
    V441 removed the cause the earlier logs showed - busy history captures fell
    from 952 to 26 - and the V441 log is clean for 220 s. Every later episode
    starts when the game creates a 160x272 colour swapchain, an overlay panel
    added beside the projection: 26 of them in 352 s, every second or two
    inside an episode. Each creation scheduled the one-second structural
    quarantine (swapchain_created), and on SteamVR the pass-through frames that
    follow stop the presenter, so generation stayed off and the game ran at its
    own 42-48 fps with the presenter delivering 37-50 frames a second. The
    frames carrying those overlays generate normally once the quarantine is
    over: 265-275 s have five layers on every frame and run clean. The capture
    waits that failed (2848, ERROR_BUSY without waiting) all fall inside these
    quarantines.
    
    A swapchain created mid-session now holds nothing off. Nothing in flight
    names it, and generation resources are taken when a projection layer first
    names a swapchain, so a replacement for the projection is armed by the first
    frame that uses it, which passes through and starts continuity over
    (projection_frame_generation_pending). The quarantine covered a race lazy
    arming has since removed - the reason the destroy path dropped its own
    second in September (6a05294), when the creation path was left as it was.
    Destroying a swapchain is unchanged: continuity starts over and the
    retained repeat is dropped, as before.
    
    What changes: only a session that creates a colour swapchain while it is
    already generating. An overlay costs nothing now; on Virtual Desktop it also
    removes the second-long hitch V442 left when CheekyFoveatedDLSS's menu
    opens. An application that creates its new projection swapchain before
    destroying the old one restarts continuity when it first uses it, instead
    of losing a second at the creation. One that destroys first, as MSFS 2024
    does, never reached this quarantine: the destroy clears the steady state
    it required. GenerationQuarantineReason::swapchain_created is kept, unused,
    for older logs.
    
    Test: xrfg_overlay_swapchain_steamvr creates and destroys a 160x272 overlay
    swapchain three times while the session generates on the presenter. Every
    wait stays on the presenter and 18 synthetics come through; with the
    quarantine put back, all 24 waits leave the presenter and none generate.
    
    ctest 89/89; presenter, DCS, frame-loop, pause, history, D3D11 bridge,
    overlay, swapchain destroy and budget scenarios looped eight times each.
    Not yet run in a headset.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

